{
    "title": "Honoring the Memory of Specialist Sarah Beckstrom, West Virginia Army National Guard",
    "type": "Presidential Document",
    "date": "December 09, 2025",
    "url": "https://www.govinfo.gov/content/pkg/FR-2025-12-09/pdf/2025-22423.pdf",
    "summary": "The President issued a proclamation directing flags to be flown at half\u2011staff on December 4, 2025, to honor Specialist Sarah Beckstrom of the West Virginia Army National Guard. The order applies to the White House, all public buildings, military posts and ships, and United States embassies and consulates around the world.\n\nThis action offers a public tribute to a service member\u2019s life and sacrifice. It gives Beckstrom\u2019s family, fellow Guard members, and the West Virginia community a visible sign of national respect. It also provides a shared moment of reflection for people across the country, reminding us of the individuals behind military service and uniting institutions\u2014government offices, schools, and bases\u2014in a common gesture.\n\nThere may be some downsides or practical hurdles. Agencies, schools, and businesses that follow federal guidance have to act quickly to lower and then raise flags, which can be hard with short notice. Some people may question how often half\u2011staff honors are used or feel unsure about the timing and duration, since this order was limited to a single day. Still, the proclamation is straightforward: it marks a solemn, time\u2011bound tribute intended to recognize one soldier\u2019s memory with dignity and consistency across the nation.",
